
# <type>(<scope>)!: <subject>
#
# <body>
#
# BREAKING CHANGE: <what breaks and what to do instead>
# Co-Authored-By: <name> <email>
#
# Lines starting with # are removed. Rules:
#
# Subject (first line)
#   - Conventional Commits. type: feat | fix | docs | test | refactor |
#     perf | build | ci | chore | revert
#   - scope is optional: the area touched, e.g. cli, bootstrap, adr,
#     sources, readme
#   - "!" after the scope marks a breaking change; add the footer too
#   - imperative, lower case, no full stop, at most 72 characters
#     ("add --target fallback", not "Added --target fallback.")
#
# Body (optional, after one blank line)
#   - say why and what changed for the user, not how the diff reads
#   - wrap at 72 characters; "- " bullets for separate points
#   - name the ADR when the change follows from one (ADR 0002)
#
# Footers (after one blank line)
#   - BREAKING CHANGE: required whenever the subject has "!"
#   - Co-Authored-By: for every agent or person who co-wrote the change
#
# Example:
#   feat(cli)!: package mloadout as a uv tool with a bootstrap subcommand
#
#   Move bootstrap.py into the src/mloadout package so it can be
#   installed with `uv tool install` and run without a clone.
#
#   BREAKING CHANGE: `uv run bootstrap.py` is removed. Run
#   `mloadout bootstrap` instead.
